WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.651
This is LumiRaw:

00:00:01.651 --> 00:00:05.397
a raw photo developer that runs entirely in your browser.

00:00:05.397 --> 00:00:08.813
There's nothing to install, and nothing is uploaded.

00:00:08.813 --> 00:00:11.310
Your photos never leave your computer.

00:00:11.612 --> 00:00:14.962
Drop in a raw file, and a few seconds later it's open,

00:00:14.962 --> 00:00:16.886
with a first edit already done.

00:00:16.886 --> 00:00:18.375
Exposure, white balance,

00:00:18.375 --> 00:00:22.532
colour and lens corrections are all measured from the photo itself.

00:00:22.941 --> 00:00:25.021
From there, you go step by step.

00:00:25.021 --> 00:00:25.996
First, framing:

00:00:25.996 --> 00:00:28.531
straighten the horizon, or pick a crop.

00:00:30.012 --> 00:00:31.002
Then brightness.

00:00:31.002 --> 00:00:36.140
The exposure is already set, and these three sliders lift or hold back the shadows,

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.802
midtones and highlights, each on their own.

00:00:39.202 --> 00:00:41.170
White balance works the same way.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:45.642
Drag a box over something neutral, or warm the picture up a little by hand.

00:00:46.041 --> 00:00:50.800
Before and after shows how far the photo has come from what the camera recorded.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:55.440
Every automatic correction is listed, down to the profile for this exact lens,

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.581
and any of them can be switched off.

00:00:59.479 --> 00:01:00.533
Then the fun part:

00:01:00.533 --> 00:01:01.118
the grade.

00:01:01.118 --> 00:01:04.397
Pick a look to start from, and fine-tune it with curves,

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.329
a colour mixer and colour wheels.

00:01:07.697 --> 00:01:12.310
Finally, download it at full resolution, as a JPEG, PNG, WebP,

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:13.947
or a sixteen-bit TIFF.
